From b0659ee3973d843838e1b3b09d990eece8b5e4ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:06:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): unblock PR #199 base and real-ML jobs

- transformers_worker: import SafetensorError lazily inside the save retry so
  the module imports in base (no [train]) envs; tests importorskip it.
- project_runner: dispatch non-Transformers engines (unsloth) through the
  executor factory again; the hardcoded TransformersPeftExecutor rejected
  backend.engine at preflight.
- goal lifecycle: defer_plateau keeps a rejected candidate's objective open
  while autonomous repair runs; close_deferred_plateau settles STOP_PLATEAU
  afterwards. Repair no longer crashes on a pre-terminated objective.
- real-ML smoke fixtures: trivially-met "minimum 0.0" goals stopped the
  objective before training (INCOMPLETE_EVALUATION_IDENTITY / GOALS_MET at
  gen 0). Plumbing smokes use the documented legacy_unbounded mode with a
  declared baseline protocol; the repair smoke uses an auto baseline and an
  unattainable bound and now asserts STOP_PLATEAU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019gwTtwhCKmJ1xUsRiA1Q3p
